        "evidence": "beta-decay-interpretation.md:1-17 states universality Δ_β^{nn→mix}=Δ_β^{mix→pp} 'is a consequence of the crossing coefficients being equally spaced: T_mix=½(T_pp+T_nn).' But T_mix being the midpoint only yields equal MATRIX displacements T_nn→T_mix and T_mix→T_pp; the block then applies this to V̂ values (md:45-64) where V̂_0^par=0.7684→V̂_0^dau=0.7510 (Δ=-0.0174) and V̂_1: 1.3029→1.2036 (Δ=-0.0993) — the induced observable changes are NOT equal, so 'the same universal amount Δ_β' does not hold at the observable (V̂) level even though it holds for the raw transfer matrix.",
